before we go here is one thing you can  do today to live a happier healthier and  more productive life it's part of our  partnership with Gretchen Rubin and her  award-winning podcast happier a new  study by MIT found 50% of the US  workforce is working remotely and with  62% of summer camps closed being a  parent and working from home can be a  huge challenge for some families I would  say all New York Times bestselling  author Gretchen Rubin joins us from her  home in New York City with tips on  sharing parenting duties and workspaces  during the pandemic  good morning Gretchen how can this be  done well you know it's not easy one of  the things to think about is now that  we're working from home we have more  flexibility with our schedules a lot of  us so if you have a morning person and a  night person really lean into that and  let the morning person do the chores  like getting getting everything going in  the morning when they're high-energy and  let the night person handle the end of  the day when maybe they're still feeling  more energetic and that morning person's  really dragging take advantage of those  natural energy levels all right Gretchen  but what if you are single and you don't  have the luxury of splitting chores or  keeping up with a partner's energy great  thing a lot of people do is virtual  babysitting this is what a grandparent  or another you know loving adult will  virtually babysit and so maybe they'll  read a story to a child over zoom or  they'll let the child put on a show  would tell or put on the show and so  they're under the watchful eye of an  adult while the other adult is working  in another room  it keeps the child occupied and happy  and with an adult's eye on them you know  I had a friend back in the day whose  father whenever he was reading the  newspaper that was the signal do not  disturb you say do not despair periods  are really important well yes because if  we need to focus if we need to have an  important phone call we need do not  disturb and so if you're working in a  family where there are a lot of people  around you need to make it very clear  when you need to be undisturbed and one  of the things that might help is to  rethink the work hours in the week maybe  you're gonna work in the evening maybe  you're gonna work over the weekend so  that more there's more flexibility in  when you might  get that do not disturb time for that  really high focus intensity time that we  all need yeah and if you can't get it  from putting a newspaper up you can put  Elmo on almost a terrific babysitter in  my household from time to time Gretchen  Rubin thank you very much we appreciate  it
 

